## Documentation-to-runtime comparison

### STUN URI validation and resolution — PASS

* English doc `example_config/super_mode/README.md:134`: “Both
  `stun:host:port` and `stun://host:port` URI forms are accepted” and “Hosts
  may be IP literals ... or syntactically valid DNS hostnames”; Chinese doc
  `README_zh.md:134`: “接受`stun:host:port`和`stun://host:port`兩種URI格式”
  and “主機可以是IP literal ... 或語法上合法的DNS主機名”.
* Code `mtypes/http_control.go:641-651` cuts the scheme and removes optional
  `//`; `:655-677` parses host/port, accepts an IP or `validSTUNHostname`, and
  returns without resolution. This is validation-only and does no I/O.
* English/Chinese docs `:134` say resolution happens at runtime in
  `SuperSTUNManager`; code `device/super_stun.go:120-149` parses the STUN URI,
  bypasses lookup for an IP at `:125-126`, and calls the injected resolver only
  for a hostname at `:135`.

### Polling is fallback-only — PASS

* English and Chinese docs `README.md:126` / `README_zh.md:126` state:
  “Polling is fallback-only” / “輪詢僅作為回退機制”.
* `device/super_http_client.go:401-413` starts SSE before polling;
  `:431-438` stops polling when the stream connects or events arrive; and
  `:448-459` starts polling only after stream termination before reconnect.

### Legacy rejection lists — PASS

* English and Chinese docs `:9` and `:198` list exactly `PrivKeyV4`,
  `PrivKeyV6`, `ListenPort`, `FwMark`, `API_Prefix`, `ListenPort_EdgeAPI`, and
  `ListenPort_ManageAPI`.
* `main_super.go:617-624` scans exactly those seven top-level names.
* English/Chinese docs `:175` say `LegacySuper` and
  `DynamicRoute.SuperNode` are rejected. `mtypes/http_control.go:615-621`
  rejects exactly those two Edge configuration forms.

### No generic endpoint-hostname support — PASS

* English/Chinese docs `:134` explicitly limit DNS hostname resolution to
  STUN and state that generic endpoint parsing remains IP-literal-only.
* `conn/conn.go:172-187` splits the endpoint and rejects it when
  `net.ParseIP(host) == nil`.

### No third-party STUN DNS dependency in examples — PASS

* `example_config/super_mode/EgNet_super.yaml:7-9` supplies only RFC 5737/3849
  documentation IP literals: `stun:203.0.113.10:3478` and
  `stuns:[2001:db8::10]:5349`; no third-party DNS hostname occurs.

### VPP residual risk — PASS

* English/Chinese docs `README.md:207` / `README_zh.md:207` explicitly state
  that VPP is excluded and unvalidated, no libmemif host ran `make vpp`, and
  VPP build/runtime regressions remain possible.

### Periodic STUN-refresh documentation — FAIL (stale/contradictory claim)

* English doc `README.md:134` states: “STUN refresh is one-shot at register
  time (no periodic refresh).” Chinese doc `README_zh.md:134` is semantically
  identical: “STUN刷新在註冊時一次性執行（無週期性刷新）”.
* The same English and Chinese tables instead claim at `README.md:152` /
  `README_zh.md:152`: `STUNRefreshIntervalSeconds | How often to refresh STUN
  candidates` / `STUN候選位址刷新間隔`. This is a public claim of periodic
  refresh and directly contradicts line 134.
* Runtime confirms no periodic timer: `device/super_http_runtime.go:60-93`
  invokes `runtime.refreshSTUN(ctx, snapshot.Parameters)` once at `:75`, before
  starting `Sync` and `reportLoop`; `refreshSTUN` at `:146-164` performs a
  single `Discover` call at `:150`. No periodic refresh scheduling exists in
  this flow.

The English and Chinese documents are semantically aligned with each other,
but both retain the same stale periodic-refresh table claim. Under the review
rule that any stale or overclaiming documentation statement rejects the wave,
this is a blocking failure.

