## Re-audit after documentation correction

The prior blocking inconsistency is resolved in both language versions.

* English `example_config/super_mode/README.md:152`: “Reserved: present in
  config schema but currently inert; STUN is one-shot at register time (no
  periodic refresh)”.
* Chinese `example_config/super_mode/README_zh.md:152`: “保留：存在於設定結構中
  但目前無效；STUN在註冊時一次性執行（無週期性刷新）”.
* These statements agree with the existing STUN section at English/Chinese
  `:134`, and with runtime: `device/super_http_runtime.go:75` makes the sole
  `refreshSTUN` call after registration, while `:146-164` makes one
  `Discover` call with no periodic scheduler.

Documentation-contract test evidence:

```
$ go test -race -count=1 . -run 'TestDocs'
ok  github.com/KusakabeSi/EtherGuard-VPN  1.128s
```

The passing suite includes `TestDocsSTUNRefreshReserved`
(`docs_contract_test.go:370-388`), which requires every Super-mode document
to contain `STUNRefreshIntervalSeconds` and a reserved/inert qualifier. The
existing fixture scan and gencfg verification above remain passing evidence.

## FINAL VERDICT: APPROVE
